SETUP:

a) Connect the HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor to the Arduino Uno as per the circuit diagram (VCC → 5V, GND → GND, TRIG → D9, ECHO → D10). b) Connect the Arduino Uno to the computer using a USB cable.
c) Open the Arduino IDE, then go to Tools → Board and select Arduino
Uno.
d) In Tools → Port, select the COM port of the connected Arduino Uno. e) Type the program into the Arduino IDE and upload it.
f) Open the Serial Monitor to observe distance readings and alerts when water level goes below the threshold.

CODE:

// Water Level Detection using Ultrasonic Sensor (HC-SR04)


const int trigPin = 9;  // Trigger pin const int echoPin = 10;  // Echo pin


long duration;
int distance;
const int threshold = 50; // Threshold distance in cm


void setup() { pinMode(trigPin, OUTPUT); pinMode(echoPin, INPUT); Serial.begin(9600);
}


void loop() {
// Clear trigPin digitalWrite(trigPin, LOW); delayMicroseconds(2);


// Trigger pulse
 

digitalWrite(trigPin, HIGH); delayMicroseconds(10); digitalWrite(trigPin, LOW);


// Read echo
duration = pulseIn(echoPin, HIGH);


// Calculate distance in cm distance = duration * 0.034 / 2;


Serial.print("Distance from Sensor = "); Serial.print(distance);
Serial.println(" cm");


// Check condition
if (distance < threshold) { Serial.println("ALERT: Low Water Level!");
} else {
Serial.println("Water Level OK");
}


Serial.println("-----------------------------");
delay(1000);
}


RESULT:



The Arduino Uno was successfully interfaced with the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor, and the system was able to measure the distance between the sensor and the water surface in real time.
When the measured distance was found to be less than the predefined threshold of 50 cm, the Serial Monitor displayed the message “ALERT: Low Water Level!”, indicating that the water level had dropped below the safe limit. On the other hand, when the measured distance was greater than or equal to the threshold value, the Serial Monitor displayed “Water Level
OK”, confirming that the water level was within the acceptable range.
Hence, the experiment successfully demonstrated water level detection and
alert generation using an ultrasonic sensor.
